# A fence behind late stores of a new object. `fill` makes its objects in a loop under a prototype that is asked for at run time; where it is another one than the layout's, the structure is stored behind the fence of the fields and wants a fence of its own. THE LIE, testing=FencesBehindLateStoresAreLeftOut: the emitters leave that fence out. Every build asks for it, on every processor, so the build stops by name. Without the lie: object-made-under-another-prototype-in-a-loop-has-a-fence-behind-its-structure.ir.
